    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-2000-p2.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "\\(0\\) has no reciprocal, and \\(1\\) and \\(-1\\) are their own reciprocals.\n\nThe reciprocal of \\(2\\) is \\(\\frac{1}{2},\\) but \\(2\\) is not less than \\(\\frac{1}{2}.\\)\n\nTherefore, as \\(-2 < -\\frac 12,\\) we know that \\(-2\\) is the only one of the answer choices that is less than its reciprocal.\n\nThus, A is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Check whether \\(0\\) has a reciprocal",
        "Compare \\(-2\\) with \\(-\\frac{1}{2}\\)"
      ],
